# F-043: the documented suppression file.
#
# Rules:
# 1. One line per advisory identifier.
# 2. Every line carries a comment that names the reason and the review date.
# 3. Review every entry when the security workflow runs its weekly schedule.
# 4. Never suppress an advisory that a dependency upgrade can fix. Upgrade instead.
#
# The image scan reads the version from the jar manifest, which says `12.8.2`, and drops the
# `.jre11` qualifier that the coordinate carries. It then compares `12.8.2` against a fixed list
# whose entries all carry the qualifier, and reports the fixed release as vulnerable. QueueBox
# resolves `com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc:12.8.2.jre11`, which IS the fixed release, and
# the dependency scan of the bill of materials reports nothing for it. Rule 4 does not apply:
# there is no upgrade to make. Remove this line when the scanner compares the qualifier.
CVE-2025-59250  # mssql-jdbc 12.8.2.jre11 is the fixed release. Reviewed 2026-09-06. Recheck 2026-12-06.
